From: Realme X2 Pro Linux port <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gadget: preserve the selected mode before SET_CONFIGURATION

A host can address the gadget and then stop during descriptor/config
selection, which leaves the UDC in default or address state even though
the selected mode is valid. Treating every such host failure as a fatal
mode switch downgrades the device to charging-only and prevents the
standard recovery service from reconnecting the public UDC interface.

Keep the requested mode active once the host has addressed the gadget.
Full configuration remains the normal success path, and not-attached
retains the existing offline-gadget success path.
---
diff --git a/src/gadget.rs b/src/gadget.rs
index c0bf385..00d1bc2 100644
--- a/src/gadget.rs
+++ b/src/gadget.rs
@@ -190,6 +190,18 @@ impl ConfigFsGadget {
                 );
                 return Ok(());
             }
+            /*
+             * A host can address the gadget and then stop before SET_CONFIGURATION
+             * (for example after a stale Windows port error). Keep the requested
+             * mode armed so the standard recovery service can reconnect the public
+             * UDC interface instead of downgrading the whole device to charging-only.
+             */
+            if state == "default" || state == "address" {
+                println!(
+                    "Gadget enabled; host addressed it but did not configure the interface yet"
+                );
+                return Ok(());
+            }
         }

         return Err(anyhow::anyhow!(
